From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Bootowser <b@o.local>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 19:24:40 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] [Bootowser] refuse new tabs when the profile says so

A tab opened over the kiosk page *is* the kiosk page replaced: the new
tab page is off by policy, so what appears is a blank one, and whatever
put it there now owns the screen. Three entry points can do it, and each
gets a guard keyed on one pref, bootowser.disableNewTabs:

  * BrowserDOMWindow -- window.open() and friends, which arrive with an
    nsIOpenWindowInfo, return null, the same contract the popup blocker
    honours, so page code cannot tell the difference. A plain link click
    with target="_blank" (or another named target) arrives WITHOUT one:
    the C++ link handler resolves the target and hands us the load.
    That is a navigation the page asked for on an ordinary click, not a
    popup, so it is honoured in the tab the kiosk already has instead of
    being killed -- such a link never goes dead. Frames use a different
    private method and are untouched.
  * URILoadingHelper.openLinkIn -- the modifier link gestures: Ctrl+click
    and middle-click from the content side and the chrome side alike,
    plus the context menu entries, since the trusted and web wrappers
    both delegate here. "current" (the ordinary click) and "save" (a
    download) pass through; tab, tabshifted, window and chromeless do
    not.
  * BrowserCommands.openTab -- Ctrl+T, the tab strip's "+" button and
    middle-click on the tab bar.

Unlike bootowser.build in the escape-hatch guards, this pref is a
runtime switch on purpose: new-tab refusal is an operator's config
choice (bootowser.conf's DISABLE_NEW_TABS), not a lockdown that has to
withstand the page trying, and the page cannot reach it anyway --
content cannot write chrome prefs, about:config is locked by policy,
the devtools are gone, and the control sidecar only runs fixed commands
from disk. The launcher writes the pref into a managed block of the
profile's user.js at every start, so a config edit lands on the next
restart. The default is fail-closed: a profile the launcher never
touched still refuses.

Upstream builds are unaffected -- they never carry this series -- and on
a Bootowser build with DISABLE_NEW_TABS=no the guards are inert.
---
 browser/base/content/browser-commands.js | 14 ++++++++++++++
 browser/modules/BrowserDOMWindow.sys.mjs | 24 ++++++++++++++++++++++++
 browser/modules/URILoadingHelper.sys.mjs | 17 +++++++++++++++++
 3 files changed, 55 insertions(+)

diff --git a/browser/base/content/browser-commands.js b/browser/base/content/browser-commands.js
index 3ed2ddc839..f08bd978b4 100644
--- a/browser/base/content/browser-commands.js
+++ b/browser/base/content/browser-commands.js
@@ -226,6 +226,20 @@ var BrowserCommands = {
   },
 
   openTab({ event, url } = {}) {
+    // [Bootowser] Ctrl+T, the tab strip's "+" button and middle-click on the
+    // tab bar all land here, and a tab opened over the kiosk page *is* the
+    // kiosk page replaced -- the new tab page itself is off by policy, so it
+    // is a blank one. Refuse when the profile says no new tabs. The pref is
+    // runtime rather than bootowser.build (as in the escape-hatch guards)
+    // because this one is an operator's config choice, bootowser.conf's
+    // DISABLE_NEW_TABS written into the profile by the launcher: content
+    // cannot write chrome prefs, about:config is locked by policy and the
+    // devtools are gone, so nothing inside the browser can flip it. The
+    // default is fail-closed for profiles the launcher never touched.
+    if (Services.prefs.getBoolPref("bootowser.disableNewTabs", true)) {
+      return;
+    }
+
     let werePassedURL = !!url;
     url ??= BROWSER_NEW_TAB_URL;
     let searchClipboard =
diff --git a/browser/modules/BrowserDOMWindow.sys.mjs b/browser/modules/BrowserDOMWindow.sys.mjs
index 29c5b15106..d2d4db7286 100644
--- a/browser/modules/BrowserDOMWindow.sys.mjs
+++ b/browser/modules/BrowserDOMWindow.sys.mjs
@@ -239,6 +239,30 @@ export class BrowserDOMWindow {
     aPolicyContainer,
     aSkipLoad
   ) {
+    // [Bootowser] Everything a content page asks for through window.open and
+    // friends lands here carrying an nsIOpenWindowInfo; frames go through
+    // #getContentWindowOrOpenURIInFrame below and are untouched. A tab or
+    // popup summoned over the kiosk page hides what the kiosk is showing, so
+    // page script gets null, exactly what the popup blocker returns. A link
+    // with target="_blank" (or another named target) reaches us WITHOUT an
+    // nsIOpenWindowInfo -- the C++ link handler resolves the target and hands
+    // us the load -- and that is a plain navigation the page asked for, not a
+    // popup, so it is honoured in the tab the kiosk already has instead of
+    // killing the link. The pref is runtime on purpose, unlike bootowser.build
+    // in patch 0002: this is the operator's config choice (bootowser.conf's
+    // DISABLE_NEW_TABS, written into the profile by the launcher), not a
+    // lockdown that must survive the page trying -- and the page cannot reach
+    // it: content cannot write chrome prefs, about:config is locked by policy,
+    // the devtools are gone, and the control sidecar runs fixed commands from
+    // disk. The default is fail-closed for profiles the launcher never
+    // touched.
+    if (Services.prefs.getBoolPref("bootowser.disableNewTabs", true)) {
+      if (aOpenWindowInfo || aSkipLoad) {
+        return null;
+      }
+      aWhere = Ci.nsIBrowserDOMWindow.OPEN_CURRENTWINDOW;
+    }
+
     var browsingContext = null;
     var isExternal = !!(aFlags & Ci.nsIBrowserDOMWindow.OPEN_EXTERNAL);
     var guessUserContextIdEnabled =
diff --git a/browser/modules/URILoadingHelper.sys.mjs b/browser/modules/URILoadingHelper.sys.mjs
index 9f066fe89a..36cf04c495 100644
--- a/browser/modules/URILoadingHelper.sys.mjs
+++ b/browser/modules/URILoadingHelper.sys.mjs
@@ -467,6 +467,23 @@ export const URILoadingHelper = {
       return;
     }
 
+    // [Bootowser] Every link gesture funnels through here: Ctrl+click,
+    // middle-click and target="_blank" from the content side (via
+    // ClickHandlerParent), the same from the chrome side (handleLinkClick),
+    // and the context menu's open-in-new-tab entries, since openTrustedLinkIn
+    // and openWebLinkIn both delegate to this method. "current" is an ordinary
+    // click and "save" is a download, so both pass; tab, tabshifted, window and
+    // chromeless are all "make somewhere new to put this", and the kiosk
+    // refuses them when the profile says no new tabs. See BrowserDOMWindow for
+    // why the switch is a runtime pref instead of bootowser.build.
+    if (
+      where != "current" &&
+      where != "save" &&
+      Services.prefs.getBoolPref("bootowser.disableNewTabs", true)
+    ) {
+      return;
+    }
+
     let {
       allowThirdPartyFixup,
       postData,
-- 
